-- Seed data (runs after migrations on `supabase db reset`; on a hosted project use `supabase db push --include-seed`).
-- EVERY row is PLACEHOLDER content: replace with real, checked listings before the pilot.
-- `source` starts with "PLACEHOLDER:" so none of it can be mistaken for a checked listing. Rows have stable ids
-- (md5 of the name) and `on conflict do nothing`, so re-running the seed is safe.
-- `sessions` for fixed-time experiences is [{"label": "Sat 10:00 AM"}, ...] (shape for structured fields is still open).

on conflict (id) do nothing;
